CM_ SG_ 2147545091 EstimatedPumpingPercentTorque "Estimated Pumping - Percent Torque: The calculated torque that indicates the estimated amount of torque loss due to the engine air handling system. The value transmitted in this parameter is included in SPN 514 (Nominal Friction - Percent Torque).  T...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 AtlMxmmAvllEngnPrntTrq "Actual Maximum Available Engine - Percent Torque: This is the maximum amount of torque that the engine can immediately deliver as a percentage of the reference engine torque (SPN 544).  The Actual Maximum Available Engine - Percent Torque shall take ...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 ScrThermalManagementActive "SCR Thermal Management Active: Indicates that the exhaust temperatures have been elevated for regeneration of the SCR aftertreatment system or in preparation of regeneration of the SCR aftertreatment system.00b = SCR Thermal Management is not active0...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 DpfThermalManagementActive "DPF Thermal Management Active: Indicates that the exhaust temperatures have been elevated for regeneration of the diesel particulate filter aftertreatment system or in preparation of regeneration of the diesel particulate aftertreatment system.00b = ...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 MmntrEngnMxmmPwrEnlFdk "Momentary Engine Maximum Power Enable Feedback: Momentarily requesting Engine Maximum Power Enable - feature support feedback00b = disabled01b = supported 10b = reserved11b = don't care";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 VhlAlrtnRtLmtStts "Vehicle Acceleration Rate Limit Status: Status (active or not active) of the system used to limit maximum forward vehicle acceleration.00b = Limit not active01b = Limit active10b = Reserved11b = Not availableNOTE:  The effects of emission control lim...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 AcceleratorPedal2Position "Accelerator Pedal 2 Position: The ratio of actual position of the second analog engine speed/torque request input device (such as an accelerator pedal or throttle lever) to the maximum position of the input device.  This parameter is intended for sec...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 RemoteAcceleratorPedalPosition "Remote Accelerator Pedal Position: The ratio of actual position of the remote analog engine speed/torque request input device (such as an accelerator pedal or throttle lever) to the maximum position of the input device.     For example, in on-highway...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 EnginePercentLoadAtCurrentSpeed "Engine Percent Load At Current Speed: The ratio of actual engine percent torque (indicated) to maximum indicated torque available at the current engine speed, clipped to zero torque during engine braking.";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 AcceleratorPedal1Position "Accelerator Pedal 1 Position: This parameter is intended for the primary accelerator control in an application. SPN 91 is the calculated ratio of actual position of the operator's [engine] speed request or [engine] torque request input device (most c...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 AcceleratorPedal2LowIdleSwitch "Accelerator Pedal 2 Low Idle Switch: Switch signal which indicates the state of the accelerator pedal 2 low idle switch.  The low idle switch is defined in SAE J1843.00b = Accelerator pedal 2 not in low idle condition01b = Accelerator pedal 2 in low ...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 RoadSpeedLimitStatus "Road Speed Limit Status: Status (active or not active) of the system used to limit maximum vehicle velocity.00b = Active01b = Not Active10b = Error11b = Not availableNOTE - While somewhat inconsistent with other J1939 status parameters, the states de...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 AcceleratorPedalKickdownSwitch "Accelerator Pedal Kickdown Switch: Switch signal which indicates whether the accelerator pedal kickdown switch is opened or closed.  The kickdown switch is defined in SAE J1843.00b = Kickdown passive01b = Kickdown active10b = Error11b = Not available...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545091 AcceleratorPedal1LowIdleSwitch "Accelerator Pedal 1 Low Idle Switch: Switch signal which indicates the state of the accelerator pedal 1 low idle switch.  The low idle switch is defined in SAE Recommended Practice J1843.00b = Accelerator pedal 1 not in low idle condition01b = Accele...";
CM_ BO_ 2147545092 "Electronic Engine Controller 1";
CM_ SG_ 2147545092 EngineDemandPercentTorque "Engine Demand â€“ Percent Torque: The requested torque output of the engine by all dynamic internal inputs, including smoke control, noise control and low and high speed governing.";
CM_ SG_ 2147545092 EngineStarterMode "Engine Starter Mode: There are several phases in a starting action and different reasons why a start cannot take place.0000b = start not requested0001b = starter active but not engaged0010b = starter active and engaged0011b = start finished; starter ...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545092 SrAddrssOfCntrllngDvFrEngnCntrl "Source Address of Controlling Device for Engine Control: The source address of the SAE J1939 device currently controlling the engine.  It is used to expand the torque mode parameter (see SPN 899) in cases where control is in response to an ECU that i...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545092 EngineSpeed "Engine Speed: Actual engine speed which is calculated over a minimum crankshaft angle of 720 degrees divided by the number of cylinders.";
CM_ SG_ 2147545092 ActualEnginePercentTorque "Actual Engine - Percent Torque: The calculated output torque of the engine.  The data is transmitted in indicated torque as a percent of reference engine torque (see the engine configuration message, PGN 65251).  The engine percent torque value will ...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545092 DrvrSDmndEngnPrntTrq "Driver's Demand Engine - Percent Torque: The requested torque output of the engine by the driver. It is based on input from the following requestors external to the powertrain: operator (via the accelerator pedal), cruise control and/or road speed li...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545092 AtlEngnPrntTrqFrtnl "Actual Engine - Percent Torque (Fractional): This parameter displays an additional torque in percent of the reference engine torque. When the MSB is set to 1, this parameter is not available.  When the MSB is set to 0, bits 1 to 3 indicate the desire...";
CM_ SG_ 2147545092 EngineTorqueMode "Engine Torque Mode: State signal which indicates which engine torque mode is currently generating, limiting, or controlling the torque.  Note that the modes are not in prioritized order. Not all modes may be relevant for a given device.  Some devices...";
CM_ BO_ 2147548911 "Engine Fluid Level/Pressure 1";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineCoolantLevel1 "Engine Coolant Level 1: Ratio of volume of liquid found in engine cooling system to total cooling system volume.  Typical monitoring location is in the coolant expansion tank.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineCoolantPressure1 "Engine Coolant Pressure 1: Gage pressure of liquid found in engine cooling system.See SPN 20 for alternate range and resolution.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineCrankcasePressure1 "Engine Crankcase Pressure 1: First instance of the gage pressure inside engine crankcase.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineOilPressure1 "Engine Oil Pressure 1: Gage pressure of oil in engine lubrication system as provided by oil pump.  See SPN 7468 for alternate resolution.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineOilLevel "Engine Oil Level: Ratio of current volume of engine sump oil to maximum required volume.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngnExtnddCrnksBlwBPrssr "Engine Extended Crankcase Blow-by Pressure: Differential crankcase blow-by pressure as measured through a tube with a venturi. (SPN 1264 is not to be used â€“ obsolete)";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineFuelDeliveryPressure "Engine Fuel Delivery Pressure: Gage pressure of fuel in system as delivered from supply pump to the injection pump.  See SPN 7469 for alternate resolution.See also SPN 5578 for Fuel Delivery Absolute Pressure.";
